WEBVTT

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:25.100
In the 21st century, the companies
involved in VRMMO creation

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.400
produced one virtual world after another.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.480
From alternate dimensions
to subterranean worlds,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.690
every possible setting was explored.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.940
Then, one long-established company
created a revolutionary piece of software.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.770
Incorporating an ultra-fast
general-purpose AI called R-Evo

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.100
that made NPCs no different
from actual humans;

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.230
boasting an open-ended story system
with over 10^52 branches;

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:54.810
and achieving the previously impossible
feat of reproducing all 5 senses,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.560
this game, which pursued
the ultimate realism,

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.770
entered the scene with a great splash.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:01.600
However,

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.230
video games ought to be like video games.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.770
Humans ultimately
play games for relaxation.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:13.350
There was no need for the struggles
and strife of the real world in the picture.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.100
Thus, humanity arrived at a conclusion:

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:22.020
Advanced VRMMO games are not fun.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.560
From then on, game makers
returned to non-aggravating systems,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.350
and VRMMOs steadily lost
the popularity of their golden age.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.350
Hah! Nice try!

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.270
And now my gauge is full!

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.310
The story that is about to unfold

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:47.650
takes place 10 years after the
release of that problematic game.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.010
{=1}Full Dive: This Ultimate Next-Gen Full
Dive RPG Is Even Shittier than Real Life!

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.470
VR x Reality

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.940
Faculty Room

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.940
Sorry. I still haven't decided.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.100
You're almost to your last year.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.850
Can you at least decide
between college and working?

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:15.560
I want to have a real conversation
with you about something.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.310
The track meet your freshman year.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.980
No need to bring that up now--

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.940
You won't be able to move
forward if you never address it.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.440
Isn't it the reason you can't
decide your post-graduation plans?

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.560
It's not a problem, Yuki!

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.980
You just need to turn
the pain into strength!

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.060
The enthusiasm is suffocating.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:42.140
"Turning Pain Into Strength"
"Post-Graduation Plans"

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.020
He's parroting the
title of an intro book...

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.440
How easily influenced can you be?

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.060
I know it was hard! I know it must hurt!

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.940
If it had been me, I wouldn't
be able to leave the house!

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.940
But you're tough!

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.230
You've kept coming to school anyway!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.150
He's serious?

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.400
It was such a pitiful
and heartbreaking incident.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.940
I've been a teacher for
many years, but <i>that</i> was truly--

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.980
Mr. Yasuoka, that's enough--

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.520
I want you to accept what happened!

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.310
If you can't come to grips with it,

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.980
I'll accept it for you!

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.730
I have no idea how to fix this,

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.940
but I've got you!

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.440
Solidly, see?

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.150
And so for now, Yuki,

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.020
let's turn the strength
into pain and move forward!

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.900
Now you're saying it backwards!

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.010
"Turning Pain Into Strength"
"Post-Graduation Plans"

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:24.980
Is he some kind of idiot?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.560
Hiro!

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.190
Takafumi.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:43.560
Well, did the meeting help?

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.190
It was completely useless.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.350
I'm gonna go home and play a game.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:54.150
Video games are fine, but shouldn't
you do something physically active?

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.940
We could go to the
gym together if you want.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.730
No, thanks. It's not like training
my body matters anymore.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.690
But using video games to run away--

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:06.150
There's a competition
soon, right? Kick butt.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:09.480
Yeah, it's almost been two years since--

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.020
Oh... sorry...

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.270
It's fine.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.060
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:22.810
The real world really sucks.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.900
Hey, it's Hiro!

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.150
Oh, Tanishiro...

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.060
and Mishina.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:36.850
Man, what a coincidence
running into you like this!

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:39.020
Well, how could I say no?

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.190
Thanks, dude.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.560
Whoa! We can always count on Hiro!

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.520
I'll pay you back for sure.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.310
One day, definitely,
eventually, most likely.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.690
If there's someone you don't
like at school, say the word.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.350
We'll knock 'em flat for ya.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.480
The only ones I don't like
are in front of me...

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.900
Yeah, thanks.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.440
It's been a pleasure--I mean, thanks.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.480
See ya around.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.770
Today sucks.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:11.580
Finalizing Quest 22 Available Now!

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:11.980
Then again, today...

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.310
I pre-ordered FQ.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.270
One moment.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:23.850
...is the long-awaited release day
for the new <i>Finalizing Quest</i> VRMMO.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.350
That'll be 13,000 yen.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:31.520
Huh? I'm 1,000 yen short.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.560
I made sure I had plenty of extra money...

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:40.020
Did I accidentally hand
them a 10,000-yen bill?

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:46.480
I seem to be 1,000 yen short...

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.270
I... see.

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:49.980
That won't fly, will it?

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.850
No, it will not.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:54.270
I thought not...

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:00.020
That store had the lowest price
I could find on the internet.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:04.440
It'd be crazy to find
a store selling it cheaper.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:07.970
Game Shop Kisaragi

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.930
{=2}Game Shop Kisaragi

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.400
No, there's no way.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.150
"Brand New VRMMO in stock!"

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.230
For real?

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:29.560
Hey, this is the one from 3 years ago.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:39.600
Yeah, what did I expect
in a store like this?

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.150
Um, excuse me.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.480
I have a question.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:51.060
Yes, how may I help you?

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:56.270
Um, well, do you have FQ 22
in stock? It released today.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:59.270
FQ... 22?

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:03.850
Yes. It's the 22nd <i>Finalizing Quest</i> game.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.480
Wh-Why are you suddenly laughing?

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:18.350
The 22nd? How many are they gonna make?

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.520
We're only in the 21st century.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.520
I mean, really, 22?

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.730
That's more than the
century humanity is in!

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.980
Holy crap, change the title already!

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.270
Oh...

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:31.270
So then, um, is that FQ in stock?

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:32.900
Yeah, and we're talking about FQ.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.690
You're just buying it out of habit, right?

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.400
It's like with manga.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.150
You start buying them
because they're good,

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.770
but then it slowly gets worse and worse.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:43.100
But by that point you've already
bought 20, so it feels weird to just stop.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.150
So you figure you might
as well buy the next one.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.980
I mean, what the hell, man?

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.900
I-I see your point.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.600
Compared to the first FQ
I played back in elementary school,

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.940
my enjoyment is gradually lessening
with each entry in the series,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.230
and I don't expect anything to top that--

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:58.020
Hey! Hold on, hold on.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.600
You're the store clerk.
Why are you saying this to me?

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:01.730
Because it's true.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:02.850
Just answer the question.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.310
Do you have FQ in stock or not?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.310
Who really cares about that?

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:09.100
Hey, <i>I</i> care!

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.810
If you don't have it, I'm leaving.

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:12.350
Hold on there.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.350
I have the game for you.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.440
Huh? You do?

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.480
You bet I do.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.310
How much?

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.190
Ten thousand yen.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.560
Ten thousand yen exactly?

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.480
Yup.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.310
Whaddaya say?

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:33.150
F-For 10,000 yen? I'll take it!

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.600
Money please.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.520
One moment.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:40.020
It should be over here...

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.100
Here it is.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.480
Then here's the money.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.520
Thank you for your purchase.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.270
Finally.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:49.060
Wait! This isn't FQ!

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.350
Hey! Give me my money back!

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:59.850
Play that game. It's way better than FQ.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:04.310
It's a full-dive RPG that
pursues the ultimate in realism.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.480
I don't want to!

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.230
Just give me my money back!
I want my money!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:12.440
Listen up. This game is

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.850
a super hard-core
full-dive RPG for adults.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:18.850
What? F-For adults?

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:20.230
Look down here.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.900
A double Z rating?!

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.560
There's a rating above Z?

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.850
I'm 17.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:32.020
This rating just means recommended for
20 plus. It's not an absolute restriction.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:34.190
B-But I think I'll stick with FQ--

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.730
Is it fun to play such an innocent game?

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.730
This is a more stimulating experience.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:42.270
Why not <i>do it</i> ?

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.560
Huh? H-Hey, w-wait...

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.560
I'm Reona Kisaragi. Call me Reona.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.560
What's your name?

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.480
H-Hiroshi... Yuki.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:54.520
Hiro, I log in to this game frequently.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.600
I'll teach you what you need to know.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.270
Attentively and patiently.

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:09.270
I suddenly got a hot girl's number.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:10.940
What the hell am I doing?

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.690
I let her honeypot me
into buying this game.

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:16.520
Huh?

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.940
This game is ten years old?!

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.850
I cannot come to the phone right now.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.270
Leave a message after the beep.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.900
Screw thi--

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:32.520
This cost 10,000 yen...

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.230
I'm home...

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.520
What a day...

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:43.770
K-Kaede!

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.480
S-Sorry! I didn't mean to!
It was an accident!

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.770
Close the door already, you pervert!

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.060
Today sucks.

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:05.770
The VR NX console is compatible
with nearly every VR game.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.480
A 10-year-old game is no problem.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:09.980
The real problem is...

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.230
If it's lame, I'm returning it!

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.600
No matter what she tries to pull!

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:30.440
Hero! You must defeat the Demon Lord
and save the world of Auberdine!

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:34.480
She said this was a
super hard-core full-dive RPG,

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:37.400
but it seems surprisingly standard.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:41.940
First, leave the city
and head for Flora Castle.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.230
Wow.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:12:00.270
So it uses a virtual projection
based on a scan of the player's body.

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:06.940
Wow, the wind!

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.400
And all of this!

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:09.230
Good morning.

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:11.400
Great weather, isn't it?

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:15.480
The intro of a game is always so exciting!

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:20.190
Even the feel of the
handle is crazy realistic.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:23.350
This is pretty incredible!

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:26.650
Hiro, are you home?

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:29.600
So the character name
is just my username, then.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:32.020
Y-Yes. Be right--

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.650
Ow!

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.100
Wait, that hurt?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.980
The game even reproduces pain?!

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:41.940
Not that pain is
something I want in a game...

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.190
Hiro?

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:45.520
Ow!

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:47.060
S-Sorry, Hiro!

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:50.350
Are you hurt?

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:53.150
I-I'm fine.

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:58.310
Sorry. It was just taking so long.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:01.190
The quality of the skin,
and the personality...

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:05.190
For such an old game,
the graphics are incredible.

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:07.230
I-Is something wrong?

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:10.100
No matter where I look,
there's no NPC label.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:12.940
I guess those video game
elements are cut out.

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:15.770
Y-You're going to make me blush.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.940
It really is just like reality.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.560
It's so realistic you
could forget it's a game...

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.400
"Save your adventure and quit the game?"

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:26.850
Thank goodness. It's definitely a game.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:29.150
I wasn't transported to another world.

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:30.690
Hiro, are you okay?

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.690
Did you hit your head too hard?

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:34.730
Um, you're...

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:38.560
Huh? It's me, Alicia. We've
been friends since childhood.

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:41.560
A childhood friend.
So that's the backstory.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:46.650
You promised you'd help me with
the apple harvest today. Remember?

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:49.480
Oh, right. Of course.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.350
What's taking so long, Hiro?

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.400
The apples will get over-ripe.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.900
Oh, looks like we have a
"nice young man" character.

00:13:56.900 --> 00:14:00.900
Sorry, Brother. I accidentally
made Hiro hit his head.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.900
His head? That could be bad.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.650
Let your best bud, Martin, handle this.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.020
Here.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:11.020
It smells like an apple!

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.810
It really is realistic.

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:13.850
Why an apple?

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:16.100
It keeps the doctor away.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:18.440
That's for colds, not injuries.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:22.060
How do you like the quality
this year? Delicious, right?

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:23.310
It <i>is</i> delicious.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:27.350
Wait--there's taste, too?!

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:30.980
You must be hungry not to cut it first.

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:33.900
There.

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:36.270
It's seriously no
different from real life.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.900
This game might have
been a really good find!

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:42.150
Oh, right. The first screen
told me what to do.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:46.400
First, leave the city
and head for Flora Castle.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.190
Hey, how do I get to Flora Castle?

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:01.400
A-Are you crazy? Some things
aren't okay to joke about!

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:04.020
Hiro, that's not funny!

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:05.980
It wasn't a joke...

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.310
I just want to go outside the city.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:10.400
You idiot!

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:14.900
Watch what you say!
What if the City Guard hears you?

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:17.730
The City Guard? Why would that matter?

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:19.980
Hiro, stop playing around.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:22.230
We need to go to our family's farm.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:26.810
Huh? The mood's gotten all weird.

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:32.650
Sorry, but could I pick the apples later?
I'd like to go outside the city first.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:35.520
Something's wrong.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:36.900
He's not right in the head.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:40.850
But it's totally normal
to leave the city in an RPG!

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:45.770
Look, I'm going.
I'll help with the apples later.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.690
I can't wait to see
what adventure is waiti--

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:51.230
Hiro!

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:56.350
Why would you suddenly tackle me?
Aren't you supposed to be my best friend?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.020
This really hurts!

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:02.400
It's because we're best friends!
How could I let you commit ex-urbance?

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:04.310
E-Ex-urbance?

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:08.230
Hey, do you have amnesia or something?

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.650
No, of course not.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.020
I think.

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:14.020
Listen up and listen good!

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:19.600
The town of Ted is surrounded by
a giant moat to protect the citizenry.

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:23.230
All residents are prohibited
from leaving the city!

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:27.310
Except for special envoys, no one is
allowed to enter from outside, either!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:31.900
The town is sequestered from
contact with the outside world!

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:33.810
Oh, isn't that overkill?

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:37.900
Are goblins gonna attack
in a super huge group?

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.060
Is that it?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:42.730
Well, this is the first town.
Guess you have to start somewhere.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.690
I'll just go defeat them real quick.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.690
Alicia, I think...

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.650
Yeah, it might be too late...

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.480
I can hear you!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:54.850
I'm going to have to
open your eyes for you!

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.270
Oh, I see. It's an event.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:04.940
If you beat Martin handily, you get to
make a big deal of it and leave the city.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:10.730
It takes the place of a tutorial.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.770
In that case--

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.980
I-I'm bleeding! My nose is bleeding!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.270
Do you get it now?

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:32.400
That <i>hurt</i> ! You damned idiot!
Some best friend!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.850
Screw you! I don't even know you!

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:39.150
What? You've even forgotten
about the promise we made that day?

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:42.480
Under the Kenura tree?

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:47.440
Who gives a shit about
some weird-named tree?!

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:50.650
Hiro!

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:53.480
That really hurts!

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.810
Martin, violence is wrong!

00:17:56.810 --> 00:18:01.400
It's a little late for that shit!
I've already been beaten up!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:06.310
I mean, look at you. How could you
hold your own against a goblin?

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:11.560
Dammit! I'm sick of all this shit!

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:14.310
In the real world, it's just
one shitty thing after another,

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:17.230
and now I have to get beat up in a game?!

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:20.770
Dammit! Dammit!

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.190
Screw you!

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:25.020
You're a damned NPC!

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:31.230
I got you! Not so tough now!

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:38.400
M-Martin?

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.850
A-Are you okay?

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:53.150
Brother!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.980
H-He's dead!

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.940
What? But... That can't... What?

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.850
No! He's dead!

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:04.310
S-Stay calm! D-Do we
have any healing herbs?

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.560
I just said he's dead!

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.900
What good will an herb do?!

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:11.020
I-I guess none.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:14.980
Tell me, Hiro. What are you
gonna do about this? Tell me!

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:18.600
I-I didn't mean to! It was an accident!

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.150
But my brother is dead, for dead certain.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.900
He's dead with a knife stuck in him!

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:24.810
S-Sorr--

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:28.690
Hiro. Tell me, what the
hell are you gonna do?

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:31.850
Hiro, Hiro, Hiro, Hiro!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:36.020
I'm sorry!

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:45.730
Hiro, you bastard!

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.560
Don't you dare run away!

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:48.980
Oh, shit! Oh, shit! Oh, shit!

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:53.520
What the hell?
What the hell is happening?!

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:57.440
Hiro!

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.980
What the hell is happening?

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:10.940
Hiro!

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:19.100
S-Somehow I got away.

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:21.810
But I k-killed someone.

00:20:21.810 --> 00:20:26.020
Wh-What am I gonna do?

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:27.560
Wait. Hold up.

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:29.440
This is a game, right?

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:30.650
It's fine.

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:33.400
All I have to do is start over
and select "New Game"--

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:34.810
Hiro.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.810
I'm sorry!

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.310
Wait, Reona?

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:42.850
Sorry I didn't pick up the phone.
I was taking a bath.

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.520
A-A bath?

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:49.350
Now's not the time.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:50.520
What's wrong?

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.310
Reona, your...

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.480
Oh, my avatar?

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:58.980
It's a special store perk.
Only shop employees get it.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.900
Aren't perks normally for customers?

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.690
And why are you dressed like that?

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:10.270
I'm a fairy! Monsters and NPCs can't
see me. And they can't hear me, either.

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:12.480
Basically, I'm support.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:14.980
I said I'd teach you
attentively and patiently.

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:16.900
Oh, I see.

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:19.230
Did you finish picking apples?

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:22.690
Are you on a walk through the city
with your cute childhood friend?

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:28.150
Um, well, no... I think I messed up
the first quest branch...

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:33.190
Oh? Don't tell me you did something
pervy to your childhood friend.

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.190
Um, well, you see...

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.520
Wait, I'll figure it out.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.190
Oh, I didn't notice I was wearing this.

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:44.520
You noticed how the ultra realism
excludes status screens and such?

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:49.190
Well, the way to see game
progress is with the title system!

00:21:49.190 --> 00:21:50.900
Title system?

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:56.190
On this necklace you're given a title
that is appropriate to your game state.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:59.150
So right now you're...

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:05.150
T-Title: "Best Friend Killer"!

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:06.560
What?

